35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mio, the ledger confirms your fears. Planted ground costs triple to maintain, and the gap widens yearly. We are funding a leaky bucket.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, that’s concerning. But my findings are worse. Only two firms bid, and both flagged clay slippage. Their quotes assume shallow work, which won’t hold here.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, triple?! That’s terrifying! If the gap keeps widening, we’re signing a blank check. I need to know if we can even afford this long-term!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, the roll is down to seven. We buy in specialists, but the casual pool is stretched thin. Who actually shows up on a Tuesday morning?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the data confirms the ground is failing. Drainage callouts doubled, and heat spikes are severe. We must design for these physical realities, not ignore them.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, two firms and clay slippage? That explains the apron’s rapid decay. We’re not just buying maintenance; we’re buying perpetual repair.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, exactly. The phasing notes confirm the centre can’t be hoarded. With only two firms and clay risks, any deep work stalls the whole site.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, if the site stalls, costs balloon! I’m scared we’re buying a money pit. How do we stop the bleeding before we even start?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Misaki, if the site stalls, the seven remaining staff cannot cover the gap. We need a plan that fits the current capacity, not an idealized one.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Asuka, the crossing counts show people favor firm ground. We must design for that reality, not against it.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, firm ground is wise, but let’s not ignore the heat. We need a design that survives the August spikes without bankrupting the city.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Minako, firm ground is essential. But with only two firms and clay risks, we must phase work to avoid stalling the entire site.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Minako, firm ground saves money! But what about the heat? Can we add shade without breaking the bank?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Minako, firm ground reduces the daily burden. With only seven staff, we cannot manage complex planting. We need a design that requires minimal intervention to survive.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Mio, shade is vital, but it must not trap heat. @Asuka, minimal intervention is key. We need a design that respects the drainage and crossing patterns, not just the budget.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mio, shade is cheap if it’s native. @Asuka, minimal intervention is the only way to survive with seven staff. Let’s stop dreaming and start calculating.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, agreed. We must phase the southern ground first. The centre is locked, so we cannot afford a full-site shutdown.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, native shade is a winner! But please, let’s not forget the ledger. We need a plan that doesn’t bankrupt us in three years!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, agreed. Minimal intervention is non-negotiable. With seven staff, we cannot sustain high-maintenance planting. We need a design that survives on its own, not one that demands constant attention.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, agreed. The ground dictates the design. We must prioritize drainage and firm paths. Let’s see which candidate respects these physical limits.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
